Z||000007||Nashco||10-13-2001||04:01 AM||||The thing I hate about mass produced cars that are supposed to be modern muscle cars are the parts that aren't drivetrain.  The companies (not just ford) design the car so that the v6 auto will be really cheap and anybody can afford one if they want it.  So Fast Freddie goes to buy a brand new Cobra (or what have you, SS, Firebird) that has a screaming motor, trans, rear end, etc...but still the SAME CRAPPY, low quality everything else.  Yeah, you get a little bit tweaked suspension and stuff, but what about the rest of the car.  It is just disappointing sometimes to see a brand new 35,000 dollar toy that has some chincy pieces here and there.  There should be some way you can get a real car without paying a ton.  Imports seem to be better about this, just because their stuff (interiors especially) seem to be a little more soundly engineered.  I dunno...I agree, way too many mustangs and such out there.  If they were all v8s, I wouldn't have a problem, but the majority are v6 slushbox-equipped "pretty" cars that get the piss beat out of them and are a rolling heap of junk in 120k miles.  Ok, I'm done venting:P<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
