Z||000041||Mach10||10-16-2001||10:09 AM||||*snick* <BR>I suppose all your 'stang friends that know lots about cars get all their info from Motor-trend, too?<BR>*snick-snick*<P>I'm not saying that 'stangs suck. I'm saying that My v6 Fiero will deal harsh anal-justice on any <I>stock</I> v6-stang. You wanna know why?<BR>1) Weight bias. You can sit there and spin your tires for all I care<BR>2) Power to weight. 'Stangs have been and still are too heavy. The newer v6 with 190 horses is better. but not enough.<P>The P/W ratios are close. Fiero still comes out on top. He with the better launch will win. I guarantee you that I'll get the better launch. ||||reg||10
Z||000042||stsmithgt||10-16-2001||11:29 AM||||Man peoples minds get narrowed over the simplest things in life like over the enjoyment one can get out of a car.  I saw shows on the Mustang and Vette and it looks like the Vette gives you more bang for the buck, which makes it a tempting purchase if I could afford it, but it wouldn't make me hate Mustangs.  I grew up in a Ford family.  I've owned a little of everything American and rice, but not a mustang.  None of the vehicles I've had ever gave me a reason to slam other vehicles(unless they really suck).  My Dad owned three Mustangs, a 65 coupe 5spd., GT350 Shelby, and a GT500 Shelby.  The only one I got to drive was the GT350.  By the time I turned 16, he had sold the 65 and 500.  I wouldn't mind having a 66 fastback that's modified to blow the doors off my GT on the strip AND in the corners, but I'm not going to slam you all for owning a Fiero.  A little more respect towards others on this forum is in order.  <BR>There's my practical opinion on this subject.  <P>Speaking of practical, I might even sell my GT since having a pick-up would be more useful to me at this time.  Hmmmm? Think I'll start slamming Fieros <I>if</I> I sell mine?     <P>probably not...  I enjoy driving it too much.<BR>Oops. I forgot to mention, I wouldn't be gettin' one of those V6 models either.  I miss that V8 power. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000043||Formula88||10-16-2001||12:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Lol, if my mustang is a sporty tarus what is a fiero?  a mid engined metro?  ahahaha, keep it coming idiots.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, the 5.0 generation of Mustangs (79 - ???) has nothing to do with the Taurus.  It's based on the Fox body platform, so it's a sporty Fairmont, not a Taurus.  The Fairmont and Mustang share the exact same chassis.  Now, the current body styles, I don't know about them.||||reg||1
Z||000044||BlackStang95||10-16-2001||12:43 PM||||The Bottom Line<P>Any model of car will have its lovers and its haters.  I'm definitely a Mustang lover, they were great every year (except the mid 70's...and what WAS great then?).  But contrary to what you guys might think, im not a fiero hater, at all.  I don't doubt you might beat a v-6 mustang in a fiero gt but you guys talk sheit like a v-6 mustang is on the level of a geo and its really about dead even with your beloved fiero.  Because they are so even, the car with the better driver will win, or the engine in the best shape, etc. Don't show so much hate to a car that at best is a half second slower and at worst is a half second faster than your cars.  Peace.||||reg||2
